+# Switch of patch 0004: MJW_IFT_SOLVE at import selects solve_backward's IFT solve
+# for nv > 32. Unset or 0: the original, the Newton solver's blocked Cholesky, which factors H with the right-hand side
+# b as an augmented border and the corner set to 1e30 (block_cholesky), so the corner pivot sqrt(1e30 - |U^-T b|^2) is
+# NaN once |U^-T adj_qacc| > 1e15 and the back substitution spreads it to every dof. 1: the same solve of b / s, s the
+# power of two >= max |b| (1 when max |b| <= 1), its solution times s: a power of two scales every rounding step
+# exactly, so bitwise the original wherever that is finite. 2: no border (factorize, then forward and back
+# substitution: block_cholesky.create_blocked_cholesky_factorize_solve_func). The forward is unchanged in every setting.
+IFT_SOLVE = int(os.environ.get("MJW_IFT_SOLVE", "0"))
